 "titulo": "You wake up in Sparta, age 7 🛡️ Part 1 #history #shorts",
 "capa": "AGE 7: YOU LEAVE HOME",
 "descripcion": "At seven, every Spartan boy left home for the agoge. One cloak a year, a bed of river reeds, and never enough food.\n\nSource: Plutarch, Life of Lycurgus.\n\nCould you have lasted?\n\n#history #sparta #ancientgreece #historyfacts #shorts",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "You wake up in Sparta. You are seven, and today you leave home.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "When you were born, the elders of your tribe looked you over.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "A weak baby was left on Mount Taygetus. You passed.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Every Spartan boy goes to the agoge, the state's training school.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "From now on, Sparta raises you. Not your father.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "You live in a pack of boys, led by an older boy.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "He is about twenty. He gives the orders, and the punishments.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "You learn to read and write, but only what you need.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Everything else is about obeying, enduring, and winning.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "At twelve, the rules get harder.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Your hair is cut short, and you walk barefoot, even on stones.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "No tunic. One cloak, for the whole year.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Summer or winter, it makes no difference.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "You sleep on reeds you pulled from the river, by hand.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "In winter, you mix in thistle down, for a little warmth.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "And the food? Never quite enough, on purpose.",
   "pausa": 0.8
  },
  {
   "texto": "A hungry boy learns to be bold. That is the plan.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "So how do you eat? Part two, {when_next}.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
